#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * Supplier payment terms. Each verified supplier gets one of 5 terms (admin -> Suppliers -> the supplier's page): pay before shipping, when it
 * arrives at the hub, after delivery, after the return window (the default, today's rule), or 1-30 days after the supplier ships.
 * Admin Payouts, the supplier's Finance and Overview show what is owed by those terms; an order cancelled, refused or returned AFTER it was
 * paid is "to recover" and taken off the next payout. A rejected return no longer blocks payment.
 *
 *   node scripts/patch-payment-terms.js            dry run
 *   node scripts/patch-payment-terms.js --write    applies it (each changed file is saved as <file>.before-payment-terms first)
 * Then: cd services\api ; npm run migrate
 */
